# Vendored/build binaries under include/ (and anywhere else they land):
# never text-convert these on checkout. Without this, a clone with
# core.autocrlf=true relies entirely on git's own content-sniffing to
# treat them as binary -- usually correct, but not guaranteed for every
# file shape, and a corrupted .so fails silently (dlopen just refuses to
# load it, with no hint that the bytes changed).
*.so -text
*.dylib -text
*.a -text
*.sig -text

# POSIX shell scripts: keep LF everywhere, not just on the platforms
# that default to it. demo/run_demo.sh and docker/demo-entrypoint.sh
# are COPYd verbatim into the demo image by docker/Dockerfile -- a
# CRLF-converted checkout would break them inside the container
# (/bin/sh rejects \r-terminated lines).
*.sh text eol=lf
